      "sample_id": "MAT214-66d4d20d4aeec364",
      "question": "What is the definition of a groupoid?",
      "reference_answer": "A set A on which a binary operation * is defined is called Groupoid. In other words a Groupoid is closed under a given binary operation which is written as (A,*) for the groupoid A.",
