      "sample_id": "MAT214-9b3e75b3a1ab1364",
      "question": "What are the three kinds of elementary matrix operations?",
      "reference_answer": "1. Interchange two rows (or columns). 2. Multiply each element in a row (or column) by a non-zero number. 3. Multiply a row (or column) by a non-zero number and add the result to another row (or column).",
